{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Defined in habeas_sdk::procedure.\npub struct AgentInput<'i, D: Graph> {\n    pub node: &'i D::NodeId,\n    pub contents: &'i D::NodeContent,\n}\n\npub trait AgentInputRenderer<D: Graph>: Send + Sync {\n    /// Present these supplied contents without fetching replacement contents.\n    fn render(&self, input: &AgentInput<'_, D>) -> Result<String, D::Error>;\n}\n```\n\nThe application supplies the renderer through `Validator::with_agent`.\nFor inputs queued on an ask builder, rendering errors return\n`ValidationError::Graph`. When the SDK's supplied tool harness renders a\n`read_node` result, a rendering failure returns a tool error to the agent,\nwhich can continue the conversation and recover. Neither `Graph::NodeContent`\nnor `Graph::NodeId` needs serialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n- **Renderer supplied through `Validator::with_agent`, and rendering without refetching.**\n  - `validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` and `agent.rs#fn[validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` build a `Validator` with `with_agent(agent, Arc::new(Renderer))` and run it. The first also checks that no agent means `NoAgentConfigured`.\n  - `validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` queues current-node and successor inputs. It asserts the agent receives each rendered input in queue order. It also asserts the graph reads are exactly `[1,3,2,3,1]`, one read per queued input. That rules out the renderer or SDK fetching replacement contents.\n  - `agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` checks that the supplied node contents (\"source\") appear in the request's chat history.\n- **Rendering errors on queued inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.** `validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` uses `FailingRenderer` and asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded and that the agent is never invoked.\n- **Rendering failure in the `read_node` tool harness returns a tool error and the agent can recover.**\n  - `agent.rs#fn[node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` has a renderer that always fails.\n  - The agent calls `read_node`, then gets a tool result with `is_error` set, the tool name `read_node` and the message \"unsupported node contents\".\n  - The agent then submits successfully on the next turn, so `ask` returns `true`. The test also asserts that no dependency is recorded for the undelivered contents.\n- **No serialization or display bounds on `NodeContent` or `NodeId`.** In `agent.rs`, `Node(u8)` derives only `Clone, Eq, PartialEq`, with a comment saying it has no Serde or Hash implementations. `Contents(String)` has no derives. Both are used as the `Memory` graph's `NodeId` and `NodeContent` in the rendering tests above, so a bound would fail to compile. `contracts.rs` uses similar bound-free types.\n\nI found no obligation that lacks a test. The authoring test in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` also carries a `{test}` reference but is incidental.",
  "references": "48d95242ddb7fce1d88a931e6061b063ad16c2e6cc32a7d163225cf97e75b0d0",
